  "claims": [
    {
      "text": "Fang Yuan names Earth Prison among the ten earths, the unique terrains the world called by that name after the five regions became one, the two heavens combined, and the earth veins of the five regions merged. The other nine are Earth Abyss, Earth Trench, Earth Tunnel, Earth Cave, Production Earth, Flying Earth, Formation Earth, Earth Treasury, and Tomb Earth.",
      "chapters": [
        2058
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "intro",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "char_fang_yuan",
        "gu_earth_prison",
        "reg_earth_earth_abyss",
        "reg_earth_earth_trench",
        "reg_earth_earth_tunnel",
        "reg_earth_earth_cave",
        "reg_earth_production_earth",
        "reg_earth_flying_earth",
        "reg_earth_formation_earth",
        "reg_earth_earth_treasury",
        "reg_earth_tomb_earth"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Southern Border’s Paradise Earth true inheritance describes the ten earths in detail and states that they can bear the task of being earth vein nodes. Earth Prison is not among the five Fang Yuan can create while he builds an artificial earth vein; those are Earth Abyss, Earth Trench, Earth Tunnel, Production Earth, and Formation Earth, and the other five are beyond his ability at that point.",
      "chapters": [
        2142
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "earth-vein-node",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "reg_southern_border",
        "inh_paradise_earth_true_inheritance"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Mo Yao identifies the green paste on a Frost Jade Peacock’s body as the work of a rank seven Immortal Gu called Earth Prison, with black chains from a second Immortal Gu called Earth Net coiled around the same body.",
      "chapters": [
        602
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "a-gu-of-the-same-name",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "char_mo_yao",
        "char_frost_jade_peacock",
        "sys_immortal_gu",
        "gu_earth_net"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "That Gu carries this earth’s name and is not this earth.",
